course: dictionary
lesson: 11590
title: Antiquity: the distant past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them tells you which one the writer means. «The students learned about classical antiquity in history class.» Here antiquity means the distant past, especially the time of ancient Greece and Rome.
explain: «The museum's antiquities include old coins, pots and statues.» The word has changed to antiquities, the plural form, and now it means the old objects themselves. The words coins, pots and statues are clues: they are things you can hold or see.
explain: «This church has great antiquity.» Here antiquity means being very old. Swap in very old and the sentence still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
fact: Antiquity means the distant past, especially the time of ancient Greece and Rome.
fact: Antiquities are old objects and buildings from long ago, such as statues, coins and pots.
fact: Antiquity can also mean being very old, as in a church of great antiquity.
fact: Museums show antiquities from places such as Egypt, Greece and China.
fact: Stealing and selling antiquities is a crime, and some countries ask museums to return objects taken long ago.
exercise: «The museum has pots and statues from antiquity.» What does antiquity mean here? | *The distant past, long ago | A new shop in the city centre | A type of music played at parties | A small coin you find in your pocket
exercise: What are antiquities? | *Old objects from long ago, such as statues and coins | Modern phones and computers | Places where people go to swim | Books that were printed last week
exercise: Anil says «The church has great antiquity.» What does great antiquity mean? | Being very popular with visitors | Being newly painted | *Being very old | Being very large
test: «Stealing antiquities is a crime.» What is an antiquity? | A kind of sports game with rules | A type of food eaten at lunch | *An old object from long ago | A modern toy from a shop
test: In history lessons, what does classical antiquity mean? | Modern cities in Europe | A type of sport | *Ancient Greece and Rome | The future, years from now
exam: Why might a country ask a museum to return an antiquity? | Because it is too small to see | *Because it was taken long ago and belongs to that country's history | Because it is for sale in a shop | Because it is made of plastic and too new
